{"questions":[{"question_id":"lv3xmagm","content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statement (I) : <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions are 'stereospecific', indicating that they result in the formation of only one stereo-isomer as the product.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) : <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions generally result in formation of product as racemic mixtures.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>","chapter":"hydrocarbons","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-8th-april-evening-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift","permalink":"pgiven-below-are-two-statements-p-pstatement-i---jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-zjk8plpkbsjkuplt","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statement (I) : <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions are 'stereospecific', indicating that they result in the formation of only one stereo-isomer as the product.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) : <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions generally result in formation of product as racemic mixtures.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Statement (I) explains a characteristic of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Substitution Nucleophilic Bimolecular) reactions. In <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions, the attack of the nucleophile and the departure of the leaving group occur simultaneously in a single step. This reaction has a back-side attack mechanism, where the nucleophile attacks the electrophilic carbon from the opposite side of the leaving group. This back-side attack leads to the inversion of configuration at the carbon atom undergoing substitution, a phenomenon often referred to as 'Walden inversion'. Thus, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions are stereospecific, leading to the formation of a product with a specific configuration (either inversion or retention of configuration, but typically inversion in the case of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). Therefore, Statement I is true.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) concerns <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Substitution Nucleophilic Unimolecular) reactions, which proceed in two steps: first, the leaving group departs, forming a carbocation intermediate, and then the nucleophile attacks. The attack of the nucleophile can occur from either side of the planar carbocation, resulting in the formation of both enantiomers of the product. When the reactant is chiral, the product is usually a racemic mixture, consisting of equal amounts of both enantiomers, assuming that there is no steric or electronic preference for the attack on the carbocation. This makes <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions non-stereospecific. Therefore, Statement II is true as well.</p>\n<p>Based on the explanations provided, the correct answer is <strong>Option D</strong>: Both Statement I and Statement II are true.</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>नीचे दो कथन दिए गए हैं :</p>\n<p>कथन (I) : <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> अभिक्रियाएँ 'श्रिषिम विशिष्ट' हेती हैं जो यह इंगित करता है कि वे उत्पाद के रूप में केवल एक त्रिबिमसमावयव को उत्पन्न करती हैं।</p>\n<p>कथन (II) : <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> अभिक्रियाएँ प्राय: उत्पाद के रूप में रेसिमिक मिश्रण को निर्मित करती हैं।</p>\n<p>उपर्युक्त कथनों के संदर्भ में, नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त उत्तर चुने :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"दोनों कथन I एवं कथन II गलत हैं।\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"कथन I गलत है परंतु कथन II सही है।\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"कथन I सही है परंतु कथन II गलत है।\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"दोनों कथन I एवं कथन II सही हैं।"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>कथन (I) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (प्रतिस्थापन नाभिकस्नेही द्विआण्विक) अभिक्रियाओं की एक विशेषता की व्याख्या करता है। <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> अभिक्रियाओं में, नाभिकस्नेही का आक्रमण और त्यागी समूह का प्रस्थान एक ही चरण में एक साथ होता है। इस अभिक्रिया में पश्च-पार्श्व आक्रमण तंत्र होता है, जहाँ नाभिकस्नेही त्यागी समूह की विपरीत दिशा से इलेक्ट्रॉनस्नेही कार्बन पर आक्रमण करता है। यह पश्च-पार्श्व आक्रमण प्रतिस्थापित होने वाले कार्बन परमाणु पर विन्यास के प्रतिलोमन की ओर ले जाता है, जिसे प्रायः 'वाल्डन प्रतिलोमन' कहा जाता है। इस प्रकार, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> अभिक्रियाएं त्रिविम-विशिष्ट होती हैं, जो एक विशिष्ट विन्यास वाले उत्पाद के निर्माण की ओर ले जाती हैं (या तो विन्यास का प्रतिलोमन या धारण, लेकिन <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> के मामले में सामान्यतः प्रतिलोमन)। अतः, कथन I सत्य है।</p>\n<p>कथन (II) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (प्रतिस्थापन नाभिकस्नेही एकआण्विक) अभिक्रियाओं से संबंधित है, जो दो चरणों में आगे बढ़ती हैं: पहले, त्यागी समूह प्रस्थान करता है, एक कार्बोकैटायन मध्यवर्ती बनाता है, और फिर नाभिकस्नेही आक्रमण करता है। नाभिकस्नेही का आक्रमण समतलीय कार्बोकैटायन की किसी भी तरफ से हो सकता है, जिसके परिणामस्वरूप उत्पाद के दोनों एनैन्टियोमरों का निर्माण होता है। जब अभिकारक काइरल होता है, तो उत्पाद सामान्यतः रेसमी मिश्रण होता है, जिसमें दोनों एनैन्टियोमरों की समान मात्राएं होती हैं, यह मानते हुए कि कार्बोकैटायन पर आक्रमण के लिए कोई त्रिविम या इलेक्ट्रॉनिक प्राथमिकता नहीं है। यह <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> अभिक्रियाओं को गैर-त्रिविम-विशिष्ट बनाता है। अतः, कथन II भी सत्य है।</p>\n<p>प्रदान की गई व्याख्याओं के आधार पर, सही उत्तर <strong>विकल्प D</strong> है: कथन I और कथन II दोनों सत्य हैं।</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"reaction-of-alkanes","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-8th-april-evening-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>Statement (I) explains a characteristic of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Substitution Nucleophilic Bimolecular) reactions. In <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions, the attack of the nucleophile and the departure of the leaving group occur simultaneously in a single step. This reaction has a back-side attack mechanism, where the nucleophile attacks the electrophilic carbon from the opposite side of the leaving group. This back-side attack leads to the inversion of configuration at the carbon atom undergoing substitution, a phenomenon often referred to as 'Walden inversion'. Thus, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions are stereospecific, leading to the formation of a product with a specific configuration (either inversion or retention of configuration, but typically inversion in the case of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). Therefore, Statement I is true.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) concerns <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Substitution Nucleophilic Unimolecular) reactions, which proceed in two steps: first, the leaving group departs, forming a carbocation intermediate, and then the nucleophile attacks. The attack of the nucleophile can occur from either side of the planar carbocation, resulting in the formation of both enantiomers of the product. When the reactant is chiral, the product is usually a racemic mixture, consisting of equal amounts of both enantiomers, assuming that there is no steric or electronic preference for the attack on the carbocation. This makes <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.777ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1669.3 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(589,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1169.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> reactions non-stereospecific. Therefore, Statement II is true as well.</p>\n<p>Based on the explanations provided, the correct answer is <strong>Option D</strong>: Both Statement I and Statement II are true.</p>"}]}